  "id": "COMPOUND:31159 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nomitidine may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target-mediated pathways. Specifically, Nomitidine is identified as a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately act on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These compounds—2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-(3,3-Dimethylallyl)Acetophenone, (+)-Vouacapenic Acid, and 4,5-dihydro-2-methyl-3(2H)-furanone—indirectly influence the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex by targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is a common intermediate in these pathways. The shared target of Nomitidine and these compounds implies a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, which could influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Nomitidine and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Nomitidine to modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a chain of molecular interactions involving Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
